Line 87:   } catch (err) {

Thus eight spaces before // placeholder line.

We need to replace that line with multiple lines, so we should replace from `"// placeholder: clear canvas each frame"` to something bigger.

We'll create newString that includes clearing code and overlay handling. Must preserve indentation.

So new code block:

```js
        // Clear background each frame
        const canvas = document.getElementById("game");
        const ctx = canvas.getContext("2d");
        ctx.fillStyle = "#0f1320";
        ctx.fillRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);
        // Game‑over overlay
        if (phase === "gameover") {
          // Dim background
          ctx.fillStyle = "rgba(10,10,15,0.7)";
          ctx.fillRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);
          // Game Over text
          ctx.textAlign = "center";
          ctx.font = "44px ui-sans-serif, system-ui";
          ctx.fillStyle = "#ff52ae";
          ctx.fillText("Game Over", canvas.width / 2, canvas.height / 2 - 20);
          // Final score
          ctx.font = "20px ui-sans-serif, system-ui";
          ctx.fillStyle = "#e6e6f0";
          ctx.fillText(`Final score ${score}`, canvas.width / 2, canvas.height / 2 + 14);
          // Restart instructions
          ctx.font = "16px ui-sans-serif, system-ui";
          ctx.fillStyle = "#a5a5b8";
          ctx.fillText("Press R or click Restart", canvas.width / 2, canvas.height / 2 + 42);
        }
```

Note the indentation: the try block code has 8 spaces before statements. So we need to indent accordingly: each line should start with 8 spaces (or exactly same as original). Original line had 8 spaces then comment. So we should preserve 8 spaces.

Let's count: In the file, there were 8 spaces before `// placeholder: clear canvas each frame`. That is something like `'        // placeholder...'` (eight spaces). So new lines should have the same. So we start each line with eight spaces.

Thus replace oldString with newString (multi-line). We'll need to escape newlines inside JSON; but the tool will handle it as a string.

Now we also need to add code to set phase to "gameover" maybe for testing, but not necessary; the overlay will show only if phase changes. Since the user hasn't added any logic to set it, and we shouldn't break current behavior. But it's okay; overlay won't be shown.

Thus we only implement overlay rendering code.

